# Each Academy Instructor counts the Officer tokens its own controller controls, each one, and no other token: Bot1's two
# noncreature spells (Sol Ring, Gold Pan) make two Officer tokens for Bot1, and Gold Pan a Treasure token, which is no
# Officer; Bot1's Instructor is 2/3. Bot2's Instructor and Officer token add nothing to it, and Bot2's Instructor counts
# only Bot2's one token, not Bot1's two (CR 109.5: "you" is the Instructor's controller).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Academy Instructor
Sol Ring
Gold Pan
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Academy Instructor
Sol Ring
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Academy Instructor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Gold Pan.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Hand.Academy Instructor.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Academy Instructor.Power = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Academy Instructor.Power = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Officer Token.Power = 1
